! Regressions found running the "Designing Optics Using CODE V" examples
! a missing lens file is reported, and FIR without a lens refuses (crashed)
RES nosuchlens
FIR
! THI SI (image defocus): paraxial slopes, THO, FNO and exit pupil stay
! finite, and the exit pupil does not move with the defocus (was NaN)
LEN NEW
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -32.4637
PIM
FIR
THI SI -1
PXTY ALL
THO
FIR
THI SI 0
! FLY keeps the image solve and the paraxial trace follows the flipped lens:
! PIM 47.3762, SA -0.40526 (book Table 6.3; was the unflipped lens)
FLY S1..2
SUR SA
THO
! SCA rescales what the paraxial trace sees: EFL lands on 50 exactly
LEN NEW
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -50
PIM
SCA EFL 50
FIR
! TOW headless runs its commands with ordinary output (segfaulted)
TOW
FIR
GO
